# {{server}} MCP wrapper

## Why this exists

The `{{server}}` MCP server exposes {{N}} tools. Keeping them in standing context for every
session is wasteful — most sessions don't need them. This wrapper:

- Loads only when invoked by name.
- Calls exactly the MCP tools needed for {{primary use case}}.
- Shapes the result so the parent task gets a clean answer, not a raw tool dump.

## When to use

- {{Primary use case.}}
- {{Secondary use case if any.}}

## Workflow

1. {{First MCP tool call — usually a read.}}
2. {{Second MCP tool call — the action.}}
3. Format and return the relevant fields to the caller.

## Limits

- `allowed-tools` is scoped to `mcp__{{server}}__*` — this wrapper cannot call other MCP servers.
- `disable-model-invocation: true` is REQUIRED — the whole point is to keep the MCP surface off
  the standing context budget.
- For state-changing MCP calls, the user must confirm explicitly.

